(“Rumman” or the “Application”), the user agrees to these Terms and the <a href="/en/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>. The product is provided under the Rumman brand and developed by Pascoal Eti.</p><p>Rumman is intended for business management by people who are at least 18 years old and legally able to contract. Anyone using it for a company represents that they are authorized to act for that company.</p></section><section><h2>2. What Rumman provides</h2><p>Rumman organizes customers, proposals, work orders, catalog, inventory, purchasing, rentals, accounts, cash flow, documents and operational decisions according to the features actually available in the installed version.</p><p>The Application is being prepared for closed testing. Features, plans or integrations marked as in development or planned are not part of an active offer until implemented, validated and shown in the Application.</p></section><section><h2>3. Management support</h2><p>Rumman helps record facts, identify pending work and open the related module. Guided rules and Assistant responses support decisions, while relevant actions remain subject to human review and confirmation.</p><p>The Application does not replace an accountant, lawyer, financial or tax adviser, or another qualified professional. Reports, forecasts, alerts and suggestions must be checked by the user.</p></section><section><h2>4. Account and security</h2><p>The user must provide accurate information, protect credentials, manage team access and immediately report suspected unauthorized use.</p><p>Each account and workspace must respect the limits, roles and permissions shown in the Application. The user is responsible for actions performed with their credentials, without excluding investigation of a failure legally attributable to Rumman.</p></section><section><h2>5. Local data, synchronization and backup</h2><p>Rumman uses a local-first architecture. The operational database remains primarily in the device private storage. When team or synchronization is active, structured workspace records may be sent to the backend for authorized devices, as described in the Privacy Policy.</p><p>Android may include the operational database in the private Google Account backup when device backup is enabled. Android controls this service and it may not run. The user may also create an encrypted portable export when available and is responsible for the file and password.</p></section><section><h2>6. Business content and data protection</h2><p>Data and documents entered remain owned by the user or their lawful owners. When entering data about customers, employees, suppliers or third parties, the user represents that they have a proper legal basis, provide required notices and respect data subject rights.</p><p>Illegal, excessive or unnecessary content is prohibited. The user must assess additional safeguards before processing sensitive data or data about children.</p></section><section><h2>7. Assistant and artificial intelligence</h2><p>The Assistant processes a request only when the user chooses to send it. Responses may contain errors, omissions or outdated information and are not professional advice.</p><p>The user must review content and confirm actions before they affect the business. Rumman does not promise commercial, financial, tax or legal outcomes from automated guidance.</p></section><section><h2>8. Plans, trials and payments</h2><p>If Rumman offers a trial, subscription, purchase or paid module, the valid price, currency, taxes, duration, renewal, features and limits will be shown by Google Play before confirmation. This website does not replace the store offer.</p><p>Recurring billing or conversion of a trial to a paid plan will occur only when clearly disclosed and accepted in the Google Play flow. While there is no active offer in the Application, there is no purchase through this website.</p></section><section><h2>9. Cancellation, refunds and deletion</h2><p>Any subscription must be managed and canceled through Google Play. Uninstalling the Application or deleting the account does not automatically cancel store-managed billing.</p><p>Withdrawal and refunds follow applicable law and Google Play policies. Account deletion follows <a href="/en/delete-account">Delete account and data</a> and does not replace subscription cancellation.</p></section><section><h2>10. Quotas and third-party services</h2><p>Online features may have processing, storage, file size, user, company or Assistant usage limits. Applicable limits will be disclosed in the Application or offer.</p><p>Google Play, Firebase and Cloudflare may provide billing, authentication, integrity, diagnostics, infrastructure and requested processing. Their own terms apply, and their unavailability may limit the corresponding feature.</p></section><section><h2>11. Permitted use and restrictions</h2><p>Rumman may not be used for fraud, rights violations, unlawful activity, unauthorized access, malware, artificial consumption, bypassing limits or interference with product security and operation.</p><p>Reverse engineering, copying, exploiting or redistributing the Application outside what the law permits is also prohibited.</p></section><section><h2>12. Intellectual property</h2><p>The Rumman brand, Application, visual identity, code, text, interfaces and components belong to their respective owners and are protected by applicable law.</p><p>The right to use is personal, limited, revocable, non-exclusive and non-transferable. Permissions over user content are limited to what is needed to perform requested functions.</p></section><section><h2>13. Availability and evolution</h2><p>Rumman may receive fixes, improvements, security updates and interface changes. Maintenance, connectivity, device limits, third-party outages or events beyond reasonable control may temporarily affect online features.</p><p>Uninterrupted or error-free operation is not guaranteed. Material changes to a paid feature, if any, will respect the offer, applicable law and consumer rights.</p></section><section><h2>14. Responsibilities</h2><p>The user is responsible for checking entries, protecting the device, managing team access, complying with their business legal duties and keeping appropriate backups or exports.</p><p>The party responsible for Rumman is liable for direct damage proven to result from a legally attributable failure, without excluding mandatory consumer or data protection rights.</p></section><section><h2>15. Suspension, termination and changes</h2><p>Access may be suspended to protect users and infrastructure, comply with law, investigate fraud, prevent abuse or respond to a breach of these Terms. When possible and safe, the user will be informed.</p><p>These Terms may change for legal, technical or commercial reasons. Material changes will be communicated in the Application or on the website when required.</p></section><section><h2>16. Contact and governing law</h2><p>Commercial, support and privacy contact: <a href="mailto:e-mail@rumman.app.br">e-mail@rumman.app.br</a>. Developer: <a href="https://pascoal.eti.br" rel="external noopener">Pascoal Eti</a>. Technical contact: <a href="mailto:devs@pascoal.eti.br">devs@pascoal.eti.br</a>.</p><p>Brazilian law applies. Mandatory consumer jurisdiction and protections remain preserved. If one clause is invalid, the remaining clauses continue to apply to the extent permitted.</p></section></div></article></main><footer class="site-footer"><div class="wrap footer-main"><div class="footer-brand-block"><a class="brand footer-brand" href="/en/"><span class="brand-icon"><img src="/assets/icon-192.png" width="192" height="192" alt=""></span><span class="brand-name">Rumman</span></a><p>Guided intelligent Android ERP for small businesses.</p><a class="footer-contact" href="mailto:e-mail@rumman.app.br">Contact Rumman: e-mail@rumman.app.br</a><nav class="language-switcher footer-language" aria-label="Language"><span class="visually-hidden">Language</span><